  "implemented": [
    "Static and dynamic pass_object_size parameters preserve their typed size mode and native hidden ABI arguments across provider/consumer boundaries.",
    "Native lifetimebound/noescape parameter metadata, signed callback argument encodings and sentinel/null-position contracts survive interface replay and source-free consumers.",
    "Diagnose-if contracts bind typed predicates, local/template parameter identities, referenced export owners, messages, severity and warning group. Private predicate dependencies are rejected.",
    "Returns-twice, nothrow, leaf, disabled/not-tail-called entries, nomerge/noduplicate and optnone contracts retain native attribute/type identities. Native printing converts callback indices to source numbering, omits empty optional diagnostic groups, and places parameter-dependent predicates before asm labels. Object-size overload USRs preserve size mode and dynamic/static form. Diagnostic predicates deduplicate inherited copies, rebind renamed parameters while printing, and deep-import their conditions and parents into the consumer AST.",
    "Source-free consumers reject negative diagnostic-predicate calls, missing sentinels and taking the address of object-size entries. Existing nothrow cleanup prototypes now carry the native-attribute requirement."
  ],
  "scope": [
    "The native declaration printer and object-size overload USRs changed. All 238 native unit tests and 412 compiler regressions pass against the final native inputs. Runtime sources, service binaries and GNUstep binaries are unchanged; the complete five-family source/PCH runtime matrix remains recorded at source 2.91 and was not repeated here.",
    "Final frontend/package checks cover the current facade and fixtures. Focused packages cover C++20/C++23, ARC/MRC, O0/O2, normal/eager/ASan+UBSan/TSan after source removal and relocation. Full-fixture runs are three smoke configurations.",
    "Native lifetime metadata preservation does not claim complete Objective-C borrowed-flow analysis. Enable-if overload identities and broader native attribute forms remain open. No SDK archive was rebuilt."
  ],
  "accepted_sdk_version": "2.62.0",
  "sdk_rebuilt": false,
  "profile_conformance_claimed": false,
  "native_linux_aarch64_qualified": false,
  "remaining": [
    "Broader dependent lookup and unnamed contexts outside complete template-owned member graphs; unmodeled declaration contracts and general standard-library publication/implementations.",
    "General indirect/union/alias and borrowed-result precision, mutable/reference/generic/lazy callable analysis, global/foreign/MRC and exceptional ownership effects.",
    "Remaining abstract spawn/group forms, isolation/Sendable crossings and complete Strict Concurrency enforcement.",
    "Dependent/effectful/isolated and borrowed/resource keypaths; undefined nullable nonnull/scalar/aggregate result policy and Part 8 resource-union boundary.",
    "Remaining specified language/library/metaprogramming/foreign interop, required diagnostics and complete Core/Strict/Strict Concurrency/Strict System profiles.",
    "Native Linux AArch64 implementation/qualification and coordinated post-2.62 SDK delivery."
  ]
